      "kind": "instruction",
      "path": "/home/jhx/combination_coverage/results/failure_analysis/deepswe_failed_trials_n211_20261006/trials/effect-sse-httpapi-streaming__HFfgmqh/instruction.md",
      "sha256": "b9fc8403f53c0aed7e53cf7c2ca3f5df4249de5af8ac5ffc1dfc8500d21ce205",
      "bytes": 2276,
      "line_count": 38,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line": 1,
          "text": "The HttpApi framework should support endpoints that produce typed event streams via SSE."
        },
        {
          "line": 3,
          "text": "Endpoint Definition:"
        },
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": "HttpApiEndpoint provides an sse constructor and isSSE guard. Only sse() marks an endpoint as SSE; applying withSSE to a schema does not. HttpApiSchema provides withSSE and getSSE (operates on AST nodes)."
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "Handler Registration (HttpApiBuilder):"
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": "Handlers provide handleStream where the handler returns a Stream directly. Additionally, a Stream returned from handle on an SSE endpoint is auto-detected and converted to an SSE response. Capture the current Effect context and provide it to the stream before building the response, so services remai"
        },
        {
          "line": 11,
          "text": "The returned Stream becomes an SSE response with text/event-stream, no-cache, and keep-alive headers."
        },
        {
          "line": 13,
          "text": "Discriminated Union Events:"
        },
        {
          "line": 15,
          "text": "For tagged union success schemas, set SSE event: field to _tag. Support Schema.TaggedClass and wrapped (including transformed) or suspended union members when extracting union member tags."
        },
        {
          "line": 17,
          "text": "SSE Module (HttpApiSSE):"
        },
        {
          "line": 19,
          "text": "A new HttpApiSSE module exports SSEMessage ({ data, event?, id?, retry? }) and provides:"
        },
        {
          "line": 20,
          "text": "- formatMessage(msg) returns an SSE wire-format string with multi-line data support"
        },
        {
          "line": 21,
          "text": "- formatDataMessage(data) accepts any value, JSON-encodes it, and returns an SSE wire-format string"
        },
        {
          "line": 22,
          "text": "- makeEventEncoder(schema) returns a function that produces Effect<string> where the string is a formatted SSE message"
        },
        {
          "line": 23,
          "text": "- makeUnionEventEncoder(schema) same as makeEventEncoder but for unions sets event: from _tag; falls back to data-only for non-union schemas"
        },
        {
          "line": 24,
          "text": "- makeEventDecoder(schema) decodes a JSON string into a typed value via Effect"
        },
        {
          "line": 25,
          "text": "- makeUnionEventDecoder(schema) decodes an SSEMessage into a typed value via Effect, with non-union fallback"
        },
        {
          "line": 26,
          "text": "- fromStream(stream, encoder)"
        },
        {
          "line": 27,
          "text": "- toResponse(stream, encoder)"
        },
        {
          "line": 28,
          "text": "- toStream(response, decoder) buffers partial chunks across \\n\\n boundaries"
        },
        {
          "line": 30,
          "text": "Client Consumption:"
        },
        {
          "line": 32,
          "text": "SSE endpoints return a Stream instead of a plain value. The client must validate response status before streaming so error responses still fail the outer Effect."
        },
        {
          "line": 34,
          "text": "OpenApi:"
        },
        {
          "line": 36,
          "text": "SSE endpoints use text/event-stream content type with schema referencing the event type."
        },
        {
          "line": 38,
          "text": "IMPORTANT: Please work on this in a new branch from main and commit everything when you are done."
        }
      ]
    },
